% ============================================================================
% 2. Abstract
% ============================================================================
\chapter*{Abstract}
This report presents the design and implementation of an agentic AI customer support platform for e-commerce scenarios. The objective is to automate high-volume support tasks while preserving response quality, escalation safety, and contextual continuity across chat and voice channels. The system is built on a hybrid architecture: cloud LLMs (Groq and Gemini) handle high-quality reasoning, while local/offline components (Ollama, Whisper, FAISS index) support resilience and controllable fallback behavior. A multi-agent graph orchestrates Supervisor, Triage, Resolution, and Critic roles with conditional routing, revision loops, and escalation pathways. Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) injects domain knowledge from internal FAQs and live order data. Session memory is maintained using Redis (with fallback), historical analytics use MongoDB, and an Admin dashboard provides queue and intent-priority insights. Voice mode supports streaming turn detection, partial transcripts, and low-latency responses. Results show strong practical performance for demo-grade production readiness: robust order support, consistent escalation handling, and clean multi-channel behavior. Remaining work focuses on productionization, including stronger authentication, CI/CD, deeper automated testing, and external enterprise integrations.

\textbf{Keywords:} Agentic AI, LangGraph, RAG, FastAPI, WebSocket, Whisper, Ollama, Redis, MongoDB, Voice AI

