% ============================================================================
% 3. Problem Definition & Domain
% ============================================================================
\chapter{Problem Definition and Domain}
\section{Objective}
The objective is to build an autonomous customer support system capable of handling real-world order and service queries across text and voice interactions with minimal human intervention.

\section{Chosen Domain}
The chosen domain is \textbf{AI-driven E-commerce Customer Support}. It addresses high operational pressure from repetitive order tracking, delivery concerns, refund inquiries, and intent ambiguity in customer messages.

\section{Why Agentic AI}
This problem benefits from agentic AI because:
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
    \item A single prompt-response model is insufficient for robust routing, verification, and escalation.
    \item Complex queries require task decomposition and tool usage (orders API, profile memory, RAG retrieval).
    \item Multi-agent critique improves response quality, reducing hallucination and policy drift.
    \item Hybrid reasoning (cloud + local fallback) improves reliability under API or network constraints.
\end{itemize}

