% ============================================================================
% 7. Agent Planning & Orchestration
% ============================================================================
\chapter{Agent Planning and Orchestration}
\section{Planning Mechanism}
Supervisor and Triage jointly decompose user goals into structured support actions: detect intent, determine priority, choose whether to retrieve order data, retrieve RAG evidence, and decide escalation pathways.

\section{Execution Workflow}
Workflow sequence:
\begin{enumerate}[label=\arabic*.]
    \item Accept user turn from chat or voice channel.
    \item Resolve session and optional order context.
    \item Run graph: Supervisor $\rightarrow$ Triage $\rightarrow$ Resolution.
    \item Critic evaluates draft and either approves, rejects for retry, or escalates.
    \item Persist history + metadata and return response.
\end{enumerate}

\section{Agent Coordination}
Coordination is implemented as a directed state graph with conditional edges and bounded retries (Critic rejection loops back to Resolution, capped by retry logic).

% ============================================================================
% 8. Validation and Testing
% ============================================================================
\chapter{Validation and Testing of Agentic System}
\section{Unit Validation for Tools}
Core endpoints and tool contracts were validated for shape and error behavior:
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
    \item order lookup and order summary endpoints,
    \item session profile updates,
    \item admin metrics/queue/analytics,
    \item chat and voice transport paths.
\end{itemize}

\section{Trajectory Analysis}
A complex order complaint trajectory showed:
\begin{enumerate}[label=\arabic*.]
    \item Supervisor identified order-related support with urgency.
    \item Resolution fetched order details and support knowledge.
    \item Critic enforced response quality and escalation rules.
    \item Final response preserved order grounding and user clarity.
\end{enumerate}

\section{Consistency Testing}
Repeated prompts for the same order ID produced semantically stable outputs (same order status and ETA family), with minor stylistic variance expected from LLM non-determinism.

\section{Robustness and Error Handling}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
    \item Redis outage fallback for profile memory.
    \item Missing order events returns empty list when order exists.
    \item Voice turn errors return explicit user-facing guidance.
    \item Escalation path triggers when automatic resolution confidence is insufficient.
\end{itemize}

\section{RAG Evaluation Metrics}
Qualitative metrics used:
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
    \item \textbf{Answer relevance}: degree of alignment between user question and retrieved context.
    \item \textbf{Faithfulness}: response consistency with retrieved/order data.
\end{itemize}

\section{Human-in-the-Loop}
Escalation bundle supports optional human review and takeover for high-risk or unresolved sessions.

