% ============================================================================
% 10. Results and Insights
% ============================================================================
\chapter{Results and Insights}
\section{Key Findings}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
    \item Multi-agent orchestration improved answer quality over direct single-pass generation.
    \item Critic-stage validation reduced low-quality responses and improved tone consistency.
    \item RAG and live order retrieval significantly increased factual grounding.
    \item Order-context persistence improved continuity in chat and voice support sessions.
\end{itemize}

\section{Interpretation}
The architecture demonstrates that hybrid agentic systems can balance quality, speed, and reliability in customer support tasks. Most observed issues were output-format or control-flow edge cases that were fixable through targeted middleware and turn-state controls.

% ============================================================================
% 11. Conclusion
% ============================================================================
\chapter{Conclusion}
This project delivered a functional, agentic customer support platform with multi-agent reasoning, retrieval grounding, and omnichannel support. The most effective configuration combined cloud routing and critique with local fallback and local speech processing. The main takeaway is that structured orchestration plus retrieval and memory provides more dependable support behavior than isolated prompt-based assistants.

