\chapter{Data Model and Persistence Design}
\section{MongoDB Collections}
\subsection{support\_sessions}
Contains session history, message traces, and activity features used for analytics and queue rendering.

\subsection{orders}
Contains order metadata used by store/order workflows and support grounding.

\section{Redis Key Strategy}
\begin{table}[H]
\centering
\caption{Redis key patterns}
\begin{tabularx}{\textwidth}{|l|X|}
\hline
\textbf{Key Pattern} & \textbf{Usage} \\
\hline
\path|session:{id}:history| & Ordered message list for recent turn reconstruction \\
\hline
\path|session:{id}:meta| & Intent, priority, and order context metadata \\
\hline
\path|session:{id}:profile| & Customer profile attributes (name/email/phone/order context) \\
\hline
\path|support:email:queue| & Pending/processed email support queue entries \\
\hline
\end{tabularx}
\end{table}

\section{Cache Strategy}
The response cache stores approved responses by normalized key and now uses order-scoped cache keys for order-grounded requests. This avoids accidental response leakage across different orders with similar wording.

